From 29704c23ea8c35cfdfce47824c4d7e7f2b27d5d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:02:25 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] batched painting: text with LCD antialiasing by dual-source
 blending, raster-drawn text as coverage, less to upload

Text whose masks have a coverage for each colour channel is blended by channel (OpenGL 3.3,
OpenGL ES with EXT_blend_func_extended; the OpenGL RHI backend now maps the Src1 factors),
from the picture texture; where the text is not opaque the green channel alone is the
coverage, as in the raster engine's span path. Text the raster engine draws is drawn white on
black on a device that says it is a widget, and its coverage is blended here, so rotated text
and text under a path clip keep their masks by channel. The scratch image is uploaded by its
used columns; the picture texture is made when the first picture is there.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.2 via Claude Code
